; Connectivity config: Utils\Connectivity\Database reads the
; [mariadb:<instance>] sections below; src/utils/clickhouse.php reads the
; [clickhouse:<endpoint>] section at the end of this file.
;
; MariaDB sections are keyed by instance name, namespaced as [mariadb:<instance>]
; (the header is mariadb:<instance>; `DBNAME` names the schema the instance
; serves, defaulting to the bare instance name), and the connector resolves an
; instance to its [mariadb:<instance>] section:
;
;   $conn = Database::connectTo($dbname, $account)
;
; $account is this repo's single service account (declared in the shared
; pkg/roles-<GUID> package): `simox` (read-write on the primary, read on the
; replica). The connector reads the password from the <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD key
; (uppercased account name + _PASSWORD); an absent or empty value means a
; passwordless account. This repo is passwordless by policy: the security boundary is
; ZeroTier membership plus the source-IP host pin that the framework
; gen-service-accounts derives from etc/team.ini / etc/machines.ini, plus the
; client certificate the accounts demand (`require: 'X509'` in the roles
; package — every connecting machine presents a certificate signed by the
; project CA, so the same passwordless account cannot be used from a machine
; that holds no key). See doc/system/service-accounts.md and
; doc/system/machine-certs.md.
;
; This file carries prod connectivity only and is MANUALLY MAINTAINED by the
; consumer (private data: copied into etc/ as a real file by simox's
; bin/fetch-private-data in dev, shipped into the freshly swapped etc/ by the
; framework's DEPLOY_PRIVATE_FILES — see doc/system/private-config.md).
; There is no generator anymore: `ema create
; srv/<name>-<GUID>` provisions the instance's own MariaDB and prints the
; [mariadb:<instance>] section (SERVER/PORT/MYSQL_UNIX_PORT/DBNAME) for the operator
; to record here (or `ema values <instance>` recovers a lost record). The dev
; sandbox lives in var/sandbox/<name>-<guid>/reuter.ini (generated by
; 'ema sandbox srv/<name>-<GUID>'), not here. Under EMA_TARGET=sandbox the
; app layer resolves an instance to that sandbox ini by instance name (the
; schema still comes from DBNAME; prod via REUTER_INI / this file, unchanged).
;
; The <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD keys are optional consumer-side credentials (recorded
; here by hand; absent or empty = passwordless). The framework gen-service-accounts
; reconciles the account (create + drop stale, role-based, REQUIRE X509)
; against the shared pkg/roles-<GUID> declaration but does NOT write these keys
; back — this file is the manual source of truth.
;
; Two instances: `simo0` (the writable primary) and `simo1` (its read-only
; replica; replication is established by ema's replica build — see
; doc/system/replica-bootstrap.md) both serve the shared `simo` schema, so each
; section below carries `DBNAME=simo`. The single `simox` password key is
; optional (absent or empty means passwordless); `simox` is ALL on `simo0`,
; SELECT on `simo1`, and the website reads `simo1` through the same account.
;
; Transport: the section is authoritative for the 'ema' CLI. When
; MYSQL_UNIX_PORT is set, ema connects via that socket (root/unix_socket
; auth); otherwise it uses SERVER/PORT over TCP. In prod the app layer
; (Utils\Connectivity\Database) stays TCP-only: it reads SERVER/PORT (and
; MYSQL_UNIX_PORT from .env, not from this file — .env is MYSQL_*-free) and
; presents the machine's client certificate from SSL_DIR (also .env, projected
; from deploy.conf's DEPLOY_SSL_DIR — see doc/system/machine-certs.md). Its
; socket transport is the sandbox path instead: under EMA_TARGET=sandbox it
; reads MYSQL_UNIX_PORT from the sandbox instance's own
; var/sandbox/<name>-<guid>/reuter.ini section (written by 'ema sandbox') and
; connects as root over that socket, where no certificate is applied.
;
; Server verification is ON by default: the connector verifies the server
; against <SSL_DIR>/ca.crt (secure by default). A self-signed server cert
; (no CA yet) must opt out explicitly per instance with
; SSL_VERIFY_SERVER_CERT=0 (absent or '1'/'true' = verify). See
; doc/system/machine-certs.md.

[mariadb:simo0]
SERVER=10.147.x.10
PORT=3307
DBNAME=simo
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock
; SSL_VERIFY_SERVER_CERT=0   # opt out: self-signed server cert (no CA yet)

[mariadb:simo1]
SERVER=10.147.x.11
PORT=3308
DBNAME=simo
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock
; SSL_VERIFY_SERVER_CERT=0   # opt out: self-signed server cert (no CA yet)

; ClickHouse endpoint for the cron-job metrics hooks (src/utils/clickhouse.php):
; the client reads the [clickhouse:<endpoint>] section of this same file (via
; REUTER_INI), alongside the [mariadb:<instance>] sections above.
;
; A section names one endpoint: host/port of the HTTP interface plus the
; `database` whose job_runs / job_counters schema the client writes to. The
; header is a local name for the endpoint (the client reads
; [clickhouse:simo0]); it is not the database name.
;
; Endpoint and database only: no credential. The SQL user is the global
; CLICKHOUSE_USER (default `default`, a passwordless service user allowlisted
; by the server); CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD is an optional override, empty by
; default. The security boundary is ZeroTier membership plus a source-IP
; allowlist on the server, so no credential is shipped here. The client speaks
; the plaintext HTTP interface (8123) over ZeroTier, whose wire encryption
; makes TLS redundant.
;
; An absent [clickhouse:<endpoint>] section disables metrics; it never fails a
; job.

[clickhouse:simo0]
host = <CH ZeroTier IP>
port = 8123
database = <CH database>
